<title>UK: Mill demand low in Euro cotton market.</title>
<headline>Mill demand low in Euro cotton market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mill demand for raw cotton in Europe was at a predictably low ebb in view of the impending Easter holidays, brokers said.</p>
<p>However, a few buyers were still prepared to add selectively to their known summer requirements, particularly in such growths as Central Asian and African upland/medium qualities.</p>
<p>Eastern Europe was devoid of new feature and the long staple sector was generally neglected.</p>
<p>London Newsroom,. +44 171 542 7771</p>
